# Keep the build context small and the image free of state.
#
# A fresh clone on the Pi has none of this — it is all gitignored — but a build
# from a working copy would otherwise pull in a 700MB database and ~400MB of
# logs, and bake them into the image.
#
# .git is deliberately NOT excluded: scan.py's code_version() shells out to
# `git describe` and stamps the commit onto every row it writes. Without the
# repo it degrades to NULL, silently losing the provenance of every result.
# The pack is 213KB.

.venv
__pycache__
.pytest_cache
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.log
db_backups/
.env
analysis/

# Deployment artifacts run on the host from the git checkout, not inside the
# image: run-jobs.sh drives podman, and units/ is installed into systemd.
deploy/
